  "note": "Annual election of the Antrim Town Commissioners, polled Friday 15 January 1932. Nine nominations were received for the nine vacancies, all old members, so there was no election (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1932, p. 2). All nine were old members; no contest. Returned unopposed."
